{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ember uses dedicated Glimmer components to render column definitions with typed cell and header contexts. Renderer results can be primitive content or component configurations."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" vs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ember does not export one component named "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":". Instead it provides three table-aware components:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRenderCell"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRenderHeader"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRenderFooter"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use them in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".gts"},{"type":"text","value":" templates:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  FlexRenderCell,\n  FlexRenderFooter,\n  FlexRenderHeader,\n} from '@tanstack/ember-table'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"<FlexRenderHeader @header={{header}} />\n<FlexRenderCell @cell={{cell}} />\n<FlexRenderFooter @footer={{header}} />","lang":"hbs"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRenderCell"},{"type":"text","value":" selects "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":" for aggregated rows, falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", and renders nothing for grouping placeholders."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The lowercase "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender(renderable, context)"},{"type":"text","value":" export is the low-level function used underneath those components. It calls function renderers and passes primitive results through, but it cannot mount a Glimmer component by itself and does not select the correct grouped-cell renderer."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rendering-glimmer-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering Glimmer Components"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRenderComponent()"},{"type":"text","value":" from a column definition when the renderer should mount a component:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { flexRenderComponent } from '@tanstack/ember-table'\nimport StatusCell from './StatusCell.gts'\n\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('status', {\n    cell: () => flexRenderComponent(StatusCell, { emphasis: 'strong' }),\n  }),\n])","lang":"gts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The component receives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@ctx"},{"type":"text","value":" with the cell or header context and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@options"},{"type":"text","value":" with the optional configuration passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRenderComponent"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Placeholder headers and footers remain the template's layout decision. Wrap the header or footer component in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{{#unless header.isPlaceholder}}"},{"type":"text","value":" in ordinary layouts, but render it when a spanning-header layout intentionally needs its content. When calling table methods from a template, wrap them in a locally bound helper as shown in the Ember examples."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","text":"FlexRender vs flexRender","level":2},{"id":"rendering-glimmer-components","text":"Rendering Glimmer Components","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nEmber uses dedicated Glimmer components to render column definitions with typed cell and header contexts. Renderer results can be primitive content or component configurations.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\nEmber does not export one component named `FlexRender`. Instead it provides three table-aware components:\n\n- `FlexRenderCell`\n- `FlexRenderHeader`\n- `FlexRenderFooter`\n\nUse them in `.gts` templates:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  FlexRenderCell,\n  FlexRenderFooter,\n  FlexRenderHeader,\n} from '@tanstack/ember-table'\n```\n\n```hbs\n<FlexRenderHeader @header={{header}} />\n<FlexRenderCell @cell={{cell}} />\n<FlexRenderFooter @footer={{header}} />\n```\n\n`FlexRenderCell` selects `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and renders nothing for grouping placeholders.\n\nThe lowercase `flexRender(renderable, context)` export is the low-level function used underneath those components. It calls function renderers and passes primitive results through, but it cannot mount a Glimmer component by itself and does not select the correct grouped-cell renderer.\n\n## Rendering Glimmer Components\n\nReturn `flexRenderComponent()` from a column definition when the renderer should mount a component:\n\n```gts\nimport { flexRenderComponent } from '@tanstack/ember-table'\nimport StatusCell from './StatusCell.gts'\n\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('status', {\n    cell: () => flexRenderComponent(StatusCell, { emphasis: 'strong' }),\n  }),\n])\n```\n\nThe component receives `@ctx` with the cell or header context and `@options` with the optional configuration passed to `flexRenderComponent`.\n\nPlaceholder headers and footers remain the template's layout decision. Wrap the header or footer component in `{{#unless header.isPlaceholder}}` in ordinary layouts, but render it when a spanning-header layout intentionally needs its content. When calling table methods from a template, wrap them in a locally bound helper as shown in the Ember examples.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: FlexRender (Ember) Guide\n---\n\nEmber uses dedicated Glimmer components to render column definitions with typed cell and header contexts. Renderer results can be primitive content or component configurations.\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\nEmber does not export one component named `FlexRender`. Instead it provides three table-aware components:\n\n- `FlexRenderCell`\n- `FlexRenderHeader`\n- `FlexRenderFooter`\n\nUse them in `.gts` templates:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  FlexRenderCell,\n  FlexRenderFooter,\n  FlexRenderHeader,\n} from '@tanstack/ember-table'\n```\n\n```hbs\n<FlexRenderHeader @header={{header}} />\n<FlexRenderCell @cell={{cell}} />\n<FlexRenderFooter @footer={{header}} />\n```\n\n`FlexRenderCell` selects `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and renders nothing for grouping placeholders.\n\nThe lowercase `flexRender(renderable, context)` export is the low-level function used underneath those components. It calls function renderers and passes primitive results through, but it cannot mount a Glimmer component by itself and does not select the correct grouped-cell renderer.\n\n## Rendering Glimmer Components\n\nReturn `flexRenderComponent()` from a column definition when the renderer should mount a component:\n\n```gts\nimport { flexRenderComponent } from '@tanstack/ember-table'\nimport StatusCell from './StatusCell.gts'\n\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('status', {\n    cell: () => flexRenderComponent(StatusCell, { emphasis: 'strong' }),\n  }),\n])\n```\n\nThe component receives `@ctx` with the cell or header context and `@options` with the optional configuration passed to `flexRenderComponent`.\n\nPlaceholder headers and footers remain the template's layout decision. Wrap the header or footer component in `{{#unless header.isPlaceholder}}` in ordinary layouts, but render it when a spanning-header layout intentionally needs its content. When calling table methods from a template, wrap them in a locally bound helper as shown in the Ember examples.\n"}
